WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.103
A process writing too many files is refused from the next write.

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:06.983
Needs the BPF LSM active at boot, with bpf listed in the lsm= kernel parameter.

00:00:06.983 --> 00:00:13.707
Without it, a fanotify permission group refuses on at most 4,096 marked inodes, and where that cannot run the mass encryption detection and its stop remain.

00:00:13.707 --> 00:00:15.000
Check yours: ebpfsentinel-agent ebpf host-check

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:22.000
A loop writes twelve files under a watched directory. Past the count, each write is refused.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:28.000
The agent raises an alert on the refused process.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:34.000
The rule runs in enforce mode, so the writes are refused rather than counted.
